1. **A continuous method for producing a composite web comprising two metal cover layers and a plastic core arranged therebetween**, the method comprising the steps of:

   a) continuously supplying a first metal strip and a second metal strip intended to form the two metal cover layers;

   b) continuously applying, in a pretreatment line, at least one pretreatment coating to a surface of each of the first and second metal strips which is intended to face the plastic core, the pretreatment coating being suitable for promoting adhesion between the respective metal strip and the plastic core;

   c) drying and/or curing the pretreatment coating on the first and second metal strips;

   d) winding the pretreated first metal strip and the pretreated second metal strip into respective coils after application of the pretreatment coating;

   e) subsequently transporting and/or storing the coils and feeding the coils to a laminating line which is separate from the pretreatment line;

   f) in the separate laminating line, continuously unwinding the pretreated first and second metal strips from the respective coils;

   g) continuously feeding a plastic core material between the pretreated surfaces of the first and second metal strips; and

   h) continuously bonding the first and second metal strips to the plastic core material under heat and/or pressure to form the composite web.
